## Purpose

Use one bounded Fable 5 commander pass to reconcile all existing LIMS BOX/LIMS BOT Fable outputs, specs, proof and current repo state, then execute the useful delta. Do not create another general roadmap.

## Scope

Reconcile across the related LIMS repositories and canonical product truth:

- `TombStoneDash/lims-box`;
- `TombStoneDash/limsbot`;
- `TombStoneDash/lims-bot-demo` where relevant;
- clinical/public-health laboratory product and revenue work;
- water, wastewater, environmental and public-utility laboratory opportunities;
- issue #70 duplicate Vercel project/domain reconciliation;
- demo, pricing, early-access, analytics, CRM/outreach packets and current production proof;
- all accessible prior Fable/Claude outputs and abandoned implementation packets.

## Fable work

1. classify outputs as DONE, ACTIVE, BUILD_NOW, TRUE_GATE, SUPERSEDED, DUPLICATE, HOLD or KILL;
2. identify one clinical-lab revenue lane and one water/public-utility revenue lane;
3. preserve current repos/domains and avoid duplicate product surfaces;
4. produce no more than five bounded Sonnet/Codex packets;
5. dispatch machine-safe implementation, tests, demo and reconciliation work immediately.

Use Fable for cross-file/product synthesis, market/offer judgment and contradictory-plan resolution. Use Sonnet/Codex for code, tests, PRs, demo preparation, data-safe CRM tooling and domain/project inventory.

## Stops

No protected LIMS outbound send, payment, contract, production database mutation, DNS/domain transfer, secret mutation or project deletion without the named gate. Read-only production checks, repo work, draft outreach assets, event/opportunity research and PR creation are not gates.

## Terminal output

Return only verified current state, stale/duplicate outputs rejected, clinical lane, water/public-utility lane, work dispatched/completed, true gates, proof and next automatic actions.

## Incident

A production Personnel Pack request on 2026-08-26 was captured, but the internal fallback notice reported that no PDF URL is configured and manual fulfillment is required.

No applicant name, email address, organization, or request-specific PII is included here.

## Impact

- lead capture succeeds;
- the applicant does not receive the requested Personnel Pack automatically;
- support must acknowledge and fulfill each request manually;
- a configured accreditation selection cannot produce a verified download.

## Containment completed

The affected applicant received one manual acknowledgment from Tombstone Dash Gmail. Do not send a duplicate acknowledgment.

## Required repair

1. Identify the intended source-of-truth Personnel Pack PDF for each supported accreditation type.
2. Verify each asset contains only approved public/demo content and no customer data.
3. Configure the production download URL through the existing secret/configuration path.
4. Make the applicant confirmation include a working, access-controlled or public download as intended.
5. Add regression coverage for configured and missing-PDF behavior.
6. Run one production-safe external-inbox test proving the confirmation and download both work.

## Acceptance

- supported accreditation selections map to approved assets;
- no fallback/manual-fulfillment notice on the test;
- external confirmation arrives once;
- download returns the intended PDF;
- no applicant PII appears in issues, fixtures, logs, or receipts;
- production proof is timestamped before closure.

